[Chorus]
Highland highland hit the ceilidh glitch
Harpsichord's corrupted in the ditch
Caledonia meets the motherboard's scream
We're the glitched-out heirs of every Highland dream

[Bridge]
Failed calibration bagpipe scream
File not found but the reel redeems
Reboot aye we're still alive
4096-bit bonnie synth survive

[Outro]
The last piper plays through a broken screen
The reel goes on
The reel goes on
Skip skip skip
LYRICS

echo "Generating: Glitch-Hop Celtic Reels..."
mmx music generate \
  --prompt "Highland rave, traditional Scottish bagpipes trading licks with stuttering glitch-hop beats, baroque harpsichord through bit-crushers, entire track occasionally skips like a damaged disc, CD skip effects, Celtic glitch-hop" \
  --lyrics-file glitch-celtic-lyrics.txt \
  --bpm 128 \
  --key "C minor" \
  --out "${OUTDIR}/m3-05-glitch-hop-celtic.mp3" \
  --quiet --yes 2>/dev/null && \
  echo "  ✓ m3-05-glitch-hop-celtic.mp3 ($(stat -c%s ${OUTDIR}/m3-05-glitch-hop-celtic.mp3) bytes)" || \
  echo "  ✗ m3-05 FAILED"

# ============================================================
# EXPERIMENT 2: Temperature Study
# Same prompt + lyrics, different generation temperatures
# (Note: mmx music generate doesn't have --temperature, so we'll
# vary the prompt specificity instead — minimal vs maximal detail)
# ============================================================

echo ""
echo "--- Experiment 2: Prompt Specificity Extreme ---"

# Use the deep-sea lyrics for both
echo "Generating: Minimal prompt version..."
mmx music generate \
  --prompt "Bossa nova" \
  --lyrics-file deepsea-lyrics.txt \
  --bpm 85 \
  --key "F major" \
  --out "${OUTDIR}/specificity-minimal-bossa.mp3" \
  --quiet --yes 2>/dev/null && \
  echo "  ✓ specificity-minimal ($(stat -c%s ${OUTDIR}/specificity-minimal-bossa.mp3) bytes)" || \
  echo "  ✗ minimal FAILED"

echo "Generating: Maximal prompt version..."
mmx music generate \
  --prompt "Underwater bossa nova lounge, gentle nylon string guitar playing samba rhythms, slowed and chopped vaporwave production with wow and flutter, sonar pings used as metallic percussion, distant whale songs as bass-frequency drones, deep ocean reverb, bioluminescent atmosphere, influenced by Antonio Carlos Jobim and Macintosh Plus and Boards of Canada, Portuguese female vocal with breathy delivery, Tape saturation, lo-fi aesthetic, dreamlike and melancholic" \
  --lyrics-file deepsea-lyrics.txt \
  --bpm 85 \
  --key "F major" \
  --out "${OUTDIR}/specificity-maximal-bossa.mp3" \
  --quiet --yes 2>/dev/null && \
  echo "  ✓ specificity-maximal ($(stat -c%s ${OUTDIR}/specificity-maximal-bossa.mp3) bytes)" || \
  echo "  ✗ maximal FAILED"

# ============================================================
# EXPERIMENT 3: Structural tags study
# Same lyrics but with different structure tags
# ============================================================

echo ""
echo "--- Experiment 3: Structure Variations ---"

# Standard verse-chorus
cat > struct-standard.txt << 'LYRICS'
[Verse 1]
The lighthouse turns its face to the sea
Eight seconds of light then darkness again
The keeper winds the clockwork mechanism
The fog comes in thick as a dream

[Chorus]
