The light says land the rocks say danger
The keeper says I will stay

[Verse 2]
Forty million years of waves arriving
Each one a letter no one will read
The lighthouse reads them all by its turning
The keeper counts the ones that recede

[Chorus]
Here I am at the edge of the water
Here I stand where the world falls away
The light says land the rocks say danger
The keeper says I will stay

[Bridge]
The mechanism fails the light goes dark
The keeper strikes a match and holds it to the sky
A single candle in the mouth of the ocean
Saying I am here I am here I am

[Outro]
The light returns
The light returns
The light
LYRICS

# No structure tags — same lyrics minus the [Tags]
cat > struct-none.txt << 'LYRICS'
The lighthouse turns its face to the sea
Eight seconds of light then darkness again
The keeper winds the clockwork mechanism
The fog comes in thick as a dream

Here I am at the edge of the water
Here I stand where the world falls away
The light says land the rocks say danger
The keeper says I will stay

Forty million years of waves arriving
Each one a letter no one will read
The lighthouse reads them all by its turning
The keeper counts the ones that recede

Here I am at the edge of the water
Here I stand where the world falls away
The light says land the rocks say danger
